PERMITTED USES (What Students & Educators May Freely Do):
1. Academic Instruction & Demonstration:
   Permission is granted to run, demonstrate, and evaluate this simulation software
   free of charge in classrooms, university computer laboratories, lecture halls,
   and online academic sessions.
2. Coursework, Labs & Self-Study:
   Students, teaching assistants, and independent learners may freely execute,
   explore, study, and solve problems using this suite offline or online for coursework,
   lab assignments, exam preparation, and non-commercial educational research.
3. Offline Distribution for Enrolled Students:
   Instructors and institutional lab administrators may distribute unmodified copies
   of this standalone distribution (index.html, js/, css/, documentation) to enrolled
   students for academic coursework without royalty or charge.
4. Academic Citation:
   Any publication, research paper, course syllabus, or presentation referencing
   this tool must cite:
   "Sivraj P., OSSim: Operating Systems Simulation & Learning Suite, Department of
   Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, 2026."

